PRE-PARSE BODY LIMIT: NOT IMPLEMENTED — the framework buffers and spools the whole multipart body before any handler runs, so no application-level check can bound bytes already accepted. This is a residual limitation, recorded not papered over; closing it needs a server/middleware layer and is deferred to W3.
